<title>NORWAY: PGS wins $350 mln UK oil ship deal.</title>
<headline>PGS wins $350 mln UK oil ship deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian offshore services group Petroleum Geo-Services ASA said on Thursday it had won a $350 million order from U.S. oil company Conoco to construct and operate a Ramform design floating production, storage and offloading (FPSO) system.</p>
<p>The vessel will be used on the Banff oilfield development on the British continental shelf.  </p>
<p>PGS said the contract was expected to generate $350 million over the first seven years of operations.</p>
<p>The vessel hull will be constructed in Korea by Hyundai Mipo Dockyard Ltd, and the topside will be fabricated and installed in Britain.</p>
<p>The full system is expected to be delivered and ready for operation in June 1998.</p>
<p>--Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
